MODULE 10.2 : CLASSICAL BITS VS QUBITS
================================================================================

Status : Completed

Objective
---------
Understand the difference between classical bits and quantum bits (qubits) and
learn the mathematical representation of a qubit.

Concepts Learned
----------------
• Classical Bit
• Qubit
• Quantum State
• Probability Amplitudes
• Measurement
• Computational Basis States

Key Points
----------
• Classical bits store either 0 or 1.
• A qubit is represented as a linear combination of the basis states |0⟩ and |1⟩.
• The coefficients (α and β) are called probability amplitudes.
• The amplitudes satisfy the normalization condition:
  |α|² + |β|² = 1.
• Measuring a qubit produces either 0 or 1 with probabilities determined by
  the squared magnitudes of the amplitudes.

Conclusion
----------
Understanding qubits is essential before learning quantum gates, quantum
circuits, and quantum machine learning algorithms.

