MODULE 10.6 : QUANTUM CIRCUITS

Status : In Progress

Objective:
Understand how multiple quantum gates are combined to form a complete quantum circuit.

Key Concepts:

• A quantum circuit is a sequence of quantum operations applied to qubits.
• Quantum circuits contain quantum registers and may contain classical registers.
• Quantum gates manipulate the state of qubits.
• Measurement converts quantum information into classical measurement results.
• Multiple simple gates can be combined to perform more complex quantum operations.
• A circuit can be executed many times using multiple shots to estimate measurement probabilities.

Circuit Structure:

Initial Qubit State
        ↓
Quantum Gates
        ↓
Measurement
        ↓
Classical Result

